---

SCOPE: the MIT grant above covers this project's own code -- the contents of
final_firmware/, provisioner.py, and everything else authored for Project
Stump. It does NOT extend to any third-party firmware binary flashed onto a
Heltec, or staged for the browser flasher, even when a copy of this file
sits in the same /sd/tools/ folder as those binaries on a running node.
Each third-party component below carries its own, separate license, stated
next to it. If this file arrived in a folder alongside a firmware image, do
not assume this license covers that image -- check its own license.

---

This project is built on third-party components under their own licenses:

- microReticulum / uReticulum (MIT) -- https://github.com/varna9000/micropython-reticulum
  A MicroPython port of the Reticulum protocol by Mark Qvist, independently
  maintained and MIT-licensed on its own terms. Confirmed directly against
  its current repository, not assumed: this is the one actually depended on
  here, not markqvist/Reticulum below, and its MIT status doesn't depend on
  or track that repository's own licensing history at all.
- Reticulum protocol, originated by Mark Qvist -- https://github.com/markqvist/Reticulum
  Referenced here for the protocol's origin, not as a licensed dependency of
  this project. That repository itself relicensed away from MIT on 15 April
  2025 (to a custom "Reticulum License" adding use restrictions); nothing in
  this project incorporates code from it under that later license, or needs
  to, since the actual dependency is the independently-licensed µReticulum
  port above.
- RNode Firmware CE (GPL-3.0) -- https://github.com/liberatedsystems/RNode_Firmware_CE
  Flashed onto the Heltec Bridge role, used unmodified as a pre-built binary
  from its own upstream releases -- never included as source in this
  repository or in Stump_Beta_A.zip. This project's own code stays MIT
  regardless, since nothing GPL-3.0 is combined into or distributed as part
  of it; the Heltec simply runs someone else's separately-licensed firmware.
  This is also the firmware catalog.json's own "rnode-heltec-v3" browser-
  flasher entry names as its source, for staging via tools_payload/images/
  -- that folder is empty today, but see the warning in its own README.txt
  before ever placing a real binary obtained that way in it.
- microReticulum_Firmware (GPL-3.0) -- https://github.com/attermann/microReticulum_Firmware
  Same situation as RNode Firmware CE above, for the standalone Heltec
  transport role specifically: `provisioner.py` invokes `rnodeconf
  --autoinstall --fw-url` to pull this firmware directly from attermann's
  own releases and flash it as-is. A fork of markqvist/RNode_Firmware with
  the microReticulum C++ network stack integrated -- itself a different,
  separate project from microReticulum/uReticulum above despite the
  confusingly similar name; a C++ port by the same author (attermann),
  Apache-2.0 licensed on its own, not directly used by this project at all.
- esptool-js -- see esptool-js-LICENSE.txt, distributed alongside it in this
  same tools folder
